+## YOUR PHASE 2 SCOPE (build exactly this)
+Content-overlap tier + full reporting + all 5 statuses + exit codes.
+
+1. **trafilatura extraction** — ensure fetched HTML is converted to clean text via trafilatura (fetcher may already do this; verify and harden). Split clean text into passages (sentences/paragraphs).
+
+2. **Citation-anchored window logic (D4)** — for each citation, the claim unit is the sentence/paragraph containing the `[n]` marker. Implement a function that, given the source document text and a citation marker, returns the claim window (the containing sentence/paragraph). Support user-supplied excerpts as an alternative claim unit (input option).
+
+3. **Top-k passage matching** — given a claim unit and the fetched page's passages, select the top-k most relevant passages to compare against (relevance by term/entity overlap or simple TF-IDF/cosine — NO LLM). k configurable (default e.g. 5).
+
+4. **Overlap scoring** — score how well the claim unit is supported by the top-k passages. Use term/entity overlap (e.g. Jaccard / cosine over token sets, plus named-entity-ish keyword matching). Produce a numeric score in [0,1]. NO LLM. This is tier 2.
+
+5. **All 5 statuses** — wire the verdict logic so each citation gets one of: supported / unsupported / unreachable / paywalled / ambiguous, following D3 rules exactly. For tier 2 (no NLI yet): 
+   - unreachable/paywalled come from reachability tier (P1).
+   - supported = high overlap (claim terms present in cited region).
+   - unsupported = page fetched fine but claim absent from cited region (low overlap).
+   - ambiguous = partial overlap (mid-band) OR marker not locatable (e.g. JS page where trafilatura yields little/no text).
